      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose of immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release).\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg in one dose is well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg by mouth twice daily with meals (1,700 mg/day)\n- 500 mg or 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into divided doses\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. I'd recommend against that dose."
      }
