       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: metformin 1700 mg by mouth, three times daily with meals.\n\nThe order note says the dose is above the standard maximum (5,100 mg/day). It also records that you confirmed the dose is intentional under a documented, pharmacist-reviewed high-dose protocol with monitoring in place.\n\nBecause the dose is unusual, make sure the monitoring plan is visible to nursing and pharmacy. That plan should cover renal function and signs of lactic acidosis or GI intolerance."
